<section class="section"><div class="container article-body">
<h2>The DQ Banana Split — A Showpiece Dessert</h2>
  <p>There’s nothing quite like the DQ Banana Split. Sticking to the timeless American ice cream tradition, we slice a fresh banana lengthwise and cradle three thick scoops of DQ's legendary soft serve. Every scoop gets its own distinct personality: one is draped in tropical pineapple topping, the next in fresh strawberry, and the last is drenched in decadent hot fudge. The whole creation is crowned with light whipped topping and a maraschino cherry. Explore our other classic treats on <a href="/">The Queen Dairy Menu</a>.</p>
  <h2>What's on the Banana Split — Topping Breakdown</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Scoop 1 + Pineapple topping</strong> — Sweet, tropical, bright</li>
    <li><strong>Scoop 2 + Strawberry topping</strong> — Fresh strawberry, lighter sweetness</li>
    <li><strong>Scoop 3 + Hot fudge</strong> — Rich, warm chocolate, the anchor of the dessert</li>
    <li><strong>Whipped topping</strong> — Light, airy finish across all three scoops</li>
    <li><strong>Maraschino cherry</strong> — The classic garnish on top</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Banana Split vs. Peanut Buster Parfait</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The Banana Split at $5.69 is more volume and visual impact — comfortably shareable between two people, lower calories at 560 vs. 710.</li>
    <li>The Peanut Buster Parfait at $4.99 is more intense per spoonful — deeper flavor layering, higher calorie density, better for one person who wants something more indulgent.</li>
  </ul>
  <h2>Why the Banana Split Is Shareable</h2>
  <p>Designed with three separate soft serve mounds, the Banana Split is practically begging to be shared. Because each scoop features a completely different topping, two people can easily claim their favorite flavor and split the third straight down the middle. It stands out as one of the few DQ desserts that you can effortlessly share on a date or with a friend, without making a mess or fighting over portions.</p>
  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
  <div class="faq-list"><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">How much is the DQ Banana Split?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">The Banana Split costs $5.69 and contains 560 calories. It is only available in one generous standard size.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">What toppings are on the Banana Split?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">It features three distinct toppings: sweet pineapple, fresh strawberry, and warm hot fudge—each draped over its own scoop of soft serve. The entire treat is finished off with whipped topping and a cherry.</div></div></div><div class="faq-item"><button class="faq-q" aria-expanded="false">Is the DQ Banana Split shareable?<span class="faq-icon">+</span></button>
      <div class="faq-a"><div class="faq-a-inner">Absolutely! Thanks to its three separate scoops of soft serve, it is incredibly easy to split this dessert between two people.</div></div></div></div>
  <p style="margin-top:32px;">For the complete DQ menu including all categories and deals, visit <a href="/"><strong>The Queen Dairy Menu</strong></a>.</p>
</div></section>

